{
  "dom_id": "step-e3614",
  "name": "Example: Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products",
  "problem": "Write $2\\sin{15^\\circ} \\cos{15^\\circ}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{15}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{15}^{\u2218} & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot {15}^{\u2218})=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{30}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
